"""Build the exact fifth-order exclusion page from its checked certificate."""
from pathlib import Path
import html,json,re,hashlib
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;ROOT=HERE.parents[1]
def m(x,display=True):
 tag='div' if display else 'span';return f'<{tag} class="math" data-display="{str(display).lower()}" data-tex="{html.escape(x,quote=True)}"></{tag}>'
def links(items):return '<div class="proof-links">'+''.join(f'<a href="{html.escape(u,quote=True)}">{t} ↗</a>'for u,t in items)+'</div>'
def main():
 r=json.loads((HERE/'independent-verification.json').read_text());assert r['passed'] and r['positiveDiagonalCertificate']['formsHaveRankTwo']
 assert r['certificateSHA256']==hashlib.sha256((HERE/'certificate.json').read_bytes()).hexdigest()
 css=re.search(r'<style>(.*?)</style>',(ROOT/'research/t2-qec-upper/index.html').read_text(),re.S).group(1)
 css+='\n.math{max-width:100%;overflow-x:auto}.proof-step{border-left:3px solid #b8c9bd;padding-left:1.2rem;margin:2rem 0}.badge{color:#1c6253;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.08em}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}'
 b='<p class="eyebrow">Anticoherent subspaces · Exact exclusion</p><a href="../../index.html#n=14&t=5">← Catalogue entry</a><h1>Fourteen qubits: maximum pure AC order is four</h1>'
 b+='<div class="result"><span class="badge">Proved · arbitrary complex states</span>'+m(r'\boxed{K(14,t)=0\quad(t\ge5),\qquad t_{\max}(14)=4.}')+'<p>An exact three-copy positivity certificate excludes fifth-order anticoherence. The existing fourth-order radical state attains the largest possible pure-state order.</p></div>'
 b+='<section><h2>Proof in three steps</h2><div class="proof-step"><h3>1. A positive, normalized three-copy moment</h3><p>Suppose a normalized spin-seven state is fifth-order AC. Average three copies of its projector over collective rotations:</p>'+m(r'X=\int_{\mathrm{SU}(2)}(U|\psi\rangle\langle\psi|U^\dagger)^{\otimes3}\,dU,\qquad X\succeq0,\quad\operatorname{Tr}X=1.')+'<p>This moment lies on the 680-dimensional space '+m(r'\operatorname{Sym}^3(V_7)',False)+'. Vanishing multipoles give the necessary equations</p>'+m(r'\operatorname{Tr}_1[(T_{\ell0}\otimes I\otimes I)X]=0,\qquad1\le\ell\le5.')+'</div>'
 b+='<div class="proof-step"><h3>2. Forty-five equations leave two parameters</h3><p>The angular-momentum decomposition has 47 real symmetric multiplicity coordinates. Real parts preserve positivity, trace and the equations, covering arbitrary complex amplitudes. Reconstructing selected equations with integer arithmetic gives</p>'+m(r'A\mathbf b=0,\quad A\in\mathbb Z^{45\times47},\quad\operatorname{rank}A=45,\qquad\mathbf b=R\binom uv.')+'<p>The certificate supplies the complete rank-two kernel '+m(r'R',False)+'. Both ranks are checked exactly modulo the prime 1000003, and '+m(r'AR=0',False)+' is checked over the integers.</p></div>'
 b+='<div class="proof-step"><h3>3. A positive trace cannot equal a negative probability sum</h3><p>Let '+m(r'p_J=\operatorname{Tr}(\Pi_JX)',False)+' be the probability of total spin '+m(r'J',False)+' in the three-copy moment. Reconstructing the physical trace and spin projectors gives the exact identity, valid on the entire constraint kernel,</p>'+m(r'\boxed{265256992\,\operatorname{Tr}X+26961161975\,p_4+118909381500\,p_{16}=0.}')+'<p>But '+m(r'\operatorname{Tr}X=1',False)+' and '+m(r'p_4,p_{16}\ge0',False)+', so the left side is strictly positive. This contradiction excludes every fifth-order AC state. Every higher order is excluded by nesting.</p><p>The certificate also supplies two independent positivity formulations using three diagonal entries or three total-spin probabilities. All physical probabilities are reconstructed from the full spin-ladder basis.</p></div>'
 b+=links([('proof.tex','Complete LaTeX proof and explicit forms'),('../n14-t4/index.html','Exact fourth-order witness')])+'</section>'
 b+='<section><h2>Reproduce the exact certificate</h2><p>The standalone verifier reconstructs the highest-weight vectors, spin ladders, complete representation, contraction equations, ranks, kernel and positive relation. It uses only the Python standard library and imports no discovery code.</p><pre><code>python3 verify_independently.py</code></pre>'
 b+=links([('certificate.json','Exact integer certificate'),('verify_independently.py','Independent verifier'),('independent-verification.json','Successful exact verification')])+'</section>'
 b+='<section><h2>Positive control and catalogue consistency</h2><p>The known twelve-qubit icosahedral fifth-order state survives the same three-copy construction. Its fifth reduction is verified exactly; the numerical moment has trace one and contraction residual below '+m(r'10^{-15}',False)+'. This control supplements the exact proof.</p><p>Both the pure-state and subspace catalogues now exclude fifth order at fourteen qubits, and label the fourth-order witness as globally maximal in AC order. Third-order subspace dimension is a separate question; consult its current entry below.</p>'
 b+=links([('positive-control.json','Positive-control results'),('positive-control.py','Reproduce control'),('../../../anticoherent-state-catalogue/index.html#n=14&t=5','Pure-state catalogue'),('../../index.html#n=14&t=3','Third-order subspace entry')])+'</section>'
 head='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>N=14: no fifth-order AC state</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.css"><script defer src="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.js"></script><style>'+css+'</style><script>document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded",()=>document.querySelectorAll("[data-tex]").forEach(el=>{if(window.katex)el.innerHTML=katex.renderToString(el.dataset.tex,{displayMode:el.dataset.display==="true",throwOnError:false,strict:"ignore",trust:false});}));</script></head><body><main>'
 (HERE/'index.html').write_text(head+b+'</main></body></html>\n')
if __name__=='__main__':main()
